    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0480" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7463</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d356-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-19">February 19,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Welles</hi>: Reference is made to your
                    letters of February 14, 1942, regarding financial aid to China, and of February
                    17, 1942, enclosing a copy of a letter of February 16 from the Chinese Minister
                    of Foreign Affairs together with a copy of the translation of the telegram of
                    February 15 from General Chiang Kai-shek to the President.<anchor n="94"
                        xml:id="d356-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>We have been giving the problem of effecting the loan careful consideration here
                    and we are now preparing a definite plan. I hope to be able to call a meeting on
                    the matter early next week.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Morgenthau, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d356-f1" n="93" type="source" xml:id="d356-f1-content">
                <p>See also Mr. Morgenthau’s letter of February 16 to Generalissimo Chiang,
                    Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">United States Relations With
                        China</hi>, p. 479.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d356-f2" n="94" xml:id="d356-f2-content">
                <p>Letter of February 17 not printed; for its enclosures, see <ref target="#pg468"
                        >p. 468</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
